name geonames-hierarchy
# readme.txt:
#   "hierarchy.zip		: parentId, childId, type. The type 'ADM' stands for the admin hierarchy modeled by the admin1-4 codes. The other entries are entered with the user interface. The relation toponym-adm hierarchy is not included in the file, it can instead be built from the admincodes of the toponym."
# Both ids are keys of the geoname table's rows: each is read as the place it points at, and neither is in a claim.
# Every row says the parent is above the child in the hierarchy, the readme's word for the relation; a row that
# gives a type (ADM, a value of GeoNames's own list of hierarchies; most rows give none) says the parent is above the
# child in that hierarchy too.
match hierarchy.txt

tier row by \n
names parentId childId type
tier field by \t

thing row parentId
refer parentId geonames-geoname
refer childId geonames-geoname
content type
relation "hierarchy" childId
value - type
attest row childId
relate row type to childId
